{"text": " So often you start to figure out where the weaknesses are. These artificial intelligences are jagged. That's a term people throw out. They are jagged intelligences, meaning if you think of like a graph of intelligence, what would the graph be? The y-axis is like the level of intelligence and maybe the x-axis is like, I don't know, maybe it's like a bar chart. So it has like different areas of intelligence, right? Like software engineering, mathematics, accounting, art, video generation, audio, teaching, writing. Like there's all kinds of areas of intelligence or at least maybe scalar capability. The AI is not necessarily the same level of intelligence at all of them and there's gaps. So it makes like a jagged graph. And so we as humans can sometimes fill in those gaps and that's why we're still useful economically for the moment. I don't believe being useful economically is like the purpose of humanity. So I mean, I'm not necessarily scared for the outrageous amounts of abundance that I believe we're going to have.", "segments": [{"id": 0, "seek": 0, "start": 0.0, "end": 3.2, "text": " So often you start to figure out where the weaknesses are.", "tokens": [50363, 1406, 1690, 345, 923, 284, 3785, 503, 810, 262, 20256, 389, 13, 50531], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1885392299065223, "compression_ratio": 1.7272727272727273, "no_speech_prob": 0.044054869562387466, "words": [{"word": " So", "start": 0.0, "end": 0.18, "probability": 0.5342402458190918}, {"word": " often", "start": 0.18, "end": 0.46, "probability": 0.7891746163368225}, {"word": " you", "start": 0.46, "end": 0.66, "probability": 0.7895776629447937}, {"word": " start", "start": 0.66, "end": 0.84, "probability": 0.989364504814148}, {"word": " to", "start": 0.84, "end": 1.0, "probability": 0.9984115362167358}, {"word": " figure", "start": 1.0, "end": 1.14, "probability": 0.9960492253303528}, {"word": " out", "start": 1.14, "end": 1.52, "probability": 0.9981733560562134}, {"word": " where", "